A common way to handle AABB (Axis-Aligned Bounding Box) collision with a circle (or approximated circle as a box here) and find the collision normal is to find the overlap on each axis.

The overlap on X is:
`overlapX = min(ball.x + ball.r - brick.x, brick.x + brick.w - (ball.x - ball.r))`
